---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "../../components/docs/Code.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/docs/Callout.astro";
import Endpoint from "../../components/docs/Endpoint.astro";
import Params from "../../components/docs/Params.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Calls" lead="Place outbound calls, then read everything about them: status, outcome, event timeline, transcript and recording." slug="calls">
        <h2 id="lifecycle">Call lifecycle</h2>
        <p>A call moves through these statuses, and each change sends a <a href="/docs/webhooks/">webhook event</a>:</p>
        <div class="chips">
          <span class="wd-status"><span class="wd-status-dot" aria-hidden="true" />queued</span><span class="chip">→</span>
          <span class="wd-status wd-status--dialing"><span class="wd-status-dot" aria-hidden="true" />dialing</span><span class="chip">→</span>
          <span class="wd-status wd-status--live"><span class="wd-status-dot" aria-hidden="true" />in_progress</span><span class="chip">→</span>
          <span class="wd-status wd-status--done"><span class="wd-status-dot" aria-hidden="true" />completed</span>
          <span class="chip">or</span>
          <span class="wd-status wd-status--failed"><span class="wd-status-dot" aria-hidden="true" />failed</span>
        </div>

        <h2 id="create">Place a call</h2>
        <Endpoint method="POST" path="/v1/calls" />
        <p>Returns straight away with <code>"status": "queued"</code>. The worker then dials, and the call moves through the statuses above on its own.</p>
        <Params rows={[
          { name: "agent_id", type: "uuid", required: true, desc: "The agent that runs the call. It needs a telephony connection." },
          { name: "to_number", type: "string", required: true, desc: "The number to call, in E.164 format, e.g. <code>+14155550123</code>." },
          { name: "from_number", type: "string", desc: "The caller ID. Defaults to the telephony connection's number." },
          { name: "context", type: "object", desc: "Facts for this call. They are added to the agent's prompt." },
          { name: "metadata", type: "object", desc: "Your own key/value data, stored on the call. The agent never sees it." },
          { name: "tags", type: "object", desc: "Up to 25 string labels for finding calls later, e.g. <code>{\"region\": \"North\", \"motive\": \"sales\"}</code>. Keys up to 64 characters, values up to 256. The agent never sees them." },
        ]} />
        <Params title="Headers" rows={[
          { name: "Idempotency-Key", type: "string", desc: "Retrying a request with the same key returns the original call instead of dialing again." },
        ]} />
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/calls \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY" \\
  -H "Idempotency-Key: order-7741" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{
    "agent_id": "<agent-id>",
    "to_number": "+14155550123",
    "context": { "patient_name": "Priya" },
    "tags": { "region": "North", "motive": "sales" }
  }'` }, { label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20",
  "status": "queued",
  "direction": "outbound",
  "provider_call_id": null
}` }]} />

        <h2 id="get">Retrieve a call</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/calls/{id}" />
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "id": "8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20",
  "status": "completed",
  "direction": "outbound",
  "to_number": "+14155550123",
  "from_number": "+14155550100",
  "provider_call_id": "abc-123",
  "outcome": { "summary": "Confirmed for Tuesday at 3 PM" },
  "error": null,
  "error_code": null,
  "has_recording": true,
  "tags": { "region": "North", "motive": "sales" },
  "created_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:00Z",
  "started_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:04Z",
  "ended_at": "2026-10-15T10:00:42Z"
}` }]} />

        <h2 id="list">List calls</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/calls" />
        <p>Your calls, newest first. You can combine any of these query parameters:</p>
        <Params title="Query parameters" rows={[
          { name: "status", type: "string", desc: "Only calls with this status, e.g. <code>failed</code>." },
          { name: "direction", type: "string", desc: "<code>outbound</code> or <code>inbound</code>." },
          { name: "to_number, from_number", type: "string", desc: "Only calls to or from this exact number." },
          { name: "error_code", type: "string", desc: "Only calls that failed with this <a href=\"/docs/errors/#codes\">error code</a>." },
          { name: "tag", type: "string", desc: "Only calls with this tag, written <code>key:value</code>, e.g. <code>region:North</code>. Repeat it to require several tags at once." },
          { name: "since, until", type: "datetime", desc: "Only calls created in this range (ISO 8601)." },
          { name: "limit, offset", type: "int", desc: "Paging. <code>limit</code> is 50 by default, at most 200." },
        ]} />
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl "http://localhost:8000/v1/calls?status=failed&limit=20" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY"` }]} />

        <h3 id="search-tags">Find calls by tag</h3>
        <p>
          Use the same <code>tags</code> you set when placing the call. One <code>tag</code>
          parameter matches one label; add more to narrow the results to calls that have all
          of them.
        </p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "One tag", lang: "bash", code: `# all calls in the North region
curl "http://localhost:8000/v1/calls?tag=region:North" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY"` }, { label: "Several tags", lang: "bash", code: `# North region and sales motive
curl "http://localhost:8000/v1/calls?tag=region:North&tag=motive:sales" \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY"` }]} />
        <Callout kind="tip">
          Each call in the list includes its <code>tags</code>, so you don't need to fetch
          calls one by one to read them.
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="events">Event timeline</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/calls/{id}/events" />
        <p>Everything that happened on the call, in order. This is the call's audit trail.</p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `[
  { "type": "call.queued",      "ts": "…:00Z", "data": {}, "error_code": null },
  { "type": "call.dialing",     "ts": "…:00Z", "data": { "provider_call_id": "abc-123" }, "error_code": null },
  { "type": "call.in_progress", "ts": "…:04Z", "data": {}, "error_code": null },
  { "type": "call.completed",   "ts": "…:42Z", "data": { "duration_seconds": 38 }, "error_code": null }
]` }]} />

        <h2 id="transcript">Transcript</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/calls/{id}/transcript" />
        <p>What was said, turn by turn. <code>t</code> is seconds from the start of the conversation.</p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "Response", lang: "json", code: `{
  "call_id": "8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20",
  "status": "completed",
  "summary": "Confirmed for Tuesday at 3 PM",
  "transcript": [
    { "role": "assistant", "text": "Hi, this is Alex from Acme Clinic.", "t": 0.4 },
    { "role": "user",      "text": "Hi, yes, that's me.",               "t": 2.1 },
    { "role": "assistant", "text": "Great. You're confirmed for Tuesday at 3.", "t": 4.0 }
  ]
}` }]} />
        <Callout kind="note">
          The transcript and outcome are saved when the call ends. The
          <code>call.completed</code> webhook includes the outcome summary; fetch the
          transcript from this endpoint.
        </Callout>

        <h2 id="recording">Recording</h2>
        <Endpoint method="GET" path="/v1/calls/{id}/recording" />
        <p>
          The whole call as one WAV file, with both sides mixed together. Phone calls are
          recorded automatically; <code>has_recording</code> on the call tells you whether a
          recording exists.
        </p>
        <Code tabs={[{ label: "cURL", lang: "bash", code: `curl http://localhost:8000/v1/calls/8f2c4d1e-6b7a-4c2e-9f1d-3a5b7c9e1f20/recording \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OFFHOOK_KEY" -o call.wav` }]} />

</DocsLayout>
